            <div xml:id="d225-a6">

                <pb facs="0287" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg227"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Deposition of George Derr.</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States of
                        America</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">City, County, and State of New
                        York, ss:</hi></p>
                <p>George Derr, being duly sworn, says: I was born in Bremen, Germany, and came to
                    this country when I was 14 years of age, and have, since that time, lived at the
                    city of New York. I am now 24 years of age. I have followed the sea since I was
                    15 years of age.</p>
                <p>I have heard read the foregoing affidavits of William H. Brooks and Alexander
                    Renney, and declare that the contents of the same are true.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Derr.</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Sworn to before me this 12th day of March, 1894.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred’k Giblin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Notary Public, Kings
                        County</hi></signed>.</closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Certificate filed in New York County.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
